(2757874, 383766, 44453, '<td valign="top">you''ve overxeposed the foreground element with a very strong burst of flash - not sure what camera you are using but if it''s not a SLR maybe you dont have complete control over the exposure and this is a situation you shouldn''t try to take photos of <br/>- if you do have a SLR then either reduce the flash output or the apeture so that the rope is correctly exposed - and then slow the shutter speed to allow more ambient light and expose the backgtround correctly.</td>', 'you''ve overxeposed the foreground element with a very strong burst of flash - not sure what camera you are using but if it''s not a SLR maybe you dont have complete control over the exposure and this is a situation you shouldn''t try to take photos of - if you do have a SLR then either reduce the flash output or the apeture so that the rope is correctly exposed - and then slow the shutter speed to allow more ambient light and expose the backgtround correctly.', '2006-08-24 20:12:24.000000', NULL, 1),
