(2801737, 383495, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>I think the comments you received during the challenge pretty much take care of the technical issues with your entry.  One thing the voters at DPC are sticklers for is solid black backgrounds.  Your lighting of the rope is excellent and the detail visible on the rope is also very good.  <br/> <br/>As for the subject and title chosen for your entry, obviously you touched a few raw nerves, as your histogram is heavy on the 1s and 2s.  This image does not deserve a sub-five score based on its technical merits, so the subject had to play a large factor when all is said and done.  The judging was rough for any shot that wasnt extremely creative and even rougher when the subject wasnt voter friendly.  Keep shooting and I look forward to seeing more of your entries.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, I think the comments you received during the challenge pretty much take care of the technical issues with your entry.  One thing the voters at DPC are sticklers for is solid black backgrounds.  Your lighting of the rope is excellent and the detail visible on the rope is also very good.   As for the subject and title chosen for your entry, obviously you touched a few raw nerves, as your histogram is heavy on the 1s and 2s.  This image does not deserve a sub-five score based on its technical merits, so the subject had to play a large factor when all is said and done.  The judging was rough for any shot that wasnt extremely creative and even rougher when the subject wasnt voter friendly.  Keep shooting and I look forward to seeing more of your entries. Tim', '2006-09-05 20:24:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2806687, 383003, 31133, '<td valign="top">Heh. Joey''s right. I didn''t see this until just this minute - the second I saw it, I started laughing because it''s such a great title for the image and the rope is perfect! Nice work, as always JPR. Seriously. What''s up with this score? It''s crazy where it is.</td>', 'Heh. Joey''s right. I didn''t see this until just this minute - the second I saw it, I started laughing because it''s such a great title for the image and the rope is perfect! Nice work, as always JPR. Seriously. What''s up with this score? It''s crazy where it is.', '2006-09-06 18:39:10.000000', NULL, 0),
